libnfc sources - the NFC library of the Unleashed firmware (spec D.1, D.3, D.4)
=============================================================================

Vendored for the NFC worker (#392, part 3: full protocol stacks, parsers,
mfkey), as src/lib/lfrfid and src/lib/subghz were.  Nothing here is built
yet: #392 wires it into flipper/minix.mk and adds the furi shim, the
/dev/nfc HAL stubs and the host tests.  The small hand-written library of
#387 stays in src/lib/libnfc until #392 replaces or merges it.

Source: DarkFlippers/unleashed-firmware at commit
53818b18f63e105baaf37ed8eac9a7def58ec8b1 (2026-11-16), GPLv3 (as this
project), the same commit as src/lib/lfrfid and src/lib/subghz.  Every file
is copied byte for byte (checked with cmp against that commit); the commit
is named here, not in their headers, so `cmp` against a newer Unleashed
shows what changed.  Layout:

  nfc/                          all of lib/nfc (SConscript dropped): nfc.c,
                                nfc_device*, nfc_poller/listener/scanner,
                                nfc_mock.c, helpers/ (crypto1.*, the CRCs,
                                iso14443_4_layer, nxp_native_command,
                                nfc_data_generator, nfc_util) and
                                protocols/ (iso14443_3a/3b/4a/4b,
                                iso15693_3, felica, mf_classic, mf_desfire,
                                mf_plus, mf_ultralight, ntag4xx, slix,
                                st25tb, texkom, type_4_tag, emv)
  mfkey/                        applications/system/mfkey: the MIFARE
                                Classic key recovery (mfkey32 / static
                                nested): mfkey_recovery.*, state expansion,
                                bitsliced verify, batch prelude, attack,
                                dedup, its own crypto1.*; init_plugin.c and
                                application.fam are the stock app glue
  plugins/supported_cards/      applications/main/nfc/plugins: the 45 card
                                parsers (transport, hotel, toys, EMV, NDEF)
  api/gallagher, api/mosgortrans
                                applications/main/nfc/api: helpers the
                                parsers include as ../../api/...
  toolbox/                      lib/toolbox: bit_buffer, simple_array,
                                keys_dict, pretty_format, strint, hex
  bit_lib/                      lib/bit_lib (same as src/lib/lfrfid/bit_lib)
  assets/                       aid.nfc, country_code.nfc, currency_code.nfc:
                                public lookup tables (EMV AIDs, ISO codes)

Crapto1: Unleashed has no lfsr_recovery32/64.  Its mfkey recovers keys
with its own code (mfkey/mfkey_recovery.c, mfkey_state_expansion.c,
mfkey_bs_verify.c); the Crypto1 cipher itself is nfc/helpers/crypto1.c.
Those are what part 3 ports; no Crapto1 needs to be written from memory.

Not taken:
  - The key dictionaries (mf_classic_dict.nfc, mf_plus_dict.nfc,
    mf_ultralight_c_dict.nfc, mf_ultralight_aes_dict.nfc) and the parsers'
    ID lists (sev_id, sk_id, sz_id, skylanders, vendors).  D.3 lets the
    public stock dictionary in, but Unleashed's lists are longer than
    stock's and nobody has checked where the extra keys come from.  The
    code reads the user's files from /home/flipper/nfc/assets as stock
    does; stock's own mf_classic_dict.nfc can be added later from
    flipperdevices/flipperzero-firmware.
  - lib/flipper_format and lib/toolbox/stream: a shim of FlipperFormat is
    already in src/lib/subghz/shim; #392 decides whether to share it.
  - mbedTLS (aes, des, sha1; used by mf_desfire, mf_ultralight AES/3DES and
    a few parsers): Apache-2.0, not vendored here; #392 adds what it needs.
  - The GUI app (applications/main/nfc scenes, views) and furi_hal_nfc:
    on MINIX the kernel's /dev/nfc (ST25R3916, local lane #390) and the
    `nfc` command take that part.

Code with keys in it: some parsers (plugins/supported_cards) and mfkey
carry key constants or derivation code, as in the stock source.  Under
D.3 that is code, not a secret data file, and is ported like the rest.
